>> title: Braised Short Ribs, Instant Pot
>> category: Stews & Braises
>> tags: beef, wine, braise, sunday dinner, instant pot, pressure cooker
>> counters: Instant Pot
>> dish: braised-short-ribs
>> kit: Instant Pot
>> aka: instant pot short ribs, pressure cooker short ribs, braised beef short ribs
>> servings: 4
>> time: 1 hr 50 min
>> slack: forgiving — the reduction with the lid off is the one leg the pot cannot do, and it decides whether there is a sauce at all
>> washing-up: the Instant Pot, a plate for the lifted ribs
>> capacity: 2 — the Instant Pot's base, sear
>> keeps: 4 days — cold, the fat caps it and the meat firms up enough to slice instead of shred

Four pounds and not five. Bone-in ribs stacked past a 6-quart pot's fill line will not come to pressure.

>> step: season, both faces
Season @bone-in beef short ribs{4%lb}(1.8 kg; cut in 3-in lengths) with @kosher salt{1%Tbs}, @black pepper{2%tsp}.

>> step: sear 12 min, in two batches
Sear @&(~1)seasoned short ribs{} in @vegetable oil{2%Tbs} on sauté in an #Instant Pot{} for ~sear{12%min}, in two batches, standing them on the meat faces.

>> step: soften, deglaze the base clean
Soften @yellow onions{2%large}(chopped), @carrots{2%large}(chopped), @celery{2%ribs}(chopped), @garlic{6%cloves}, @tomato paste{3%Tbs} with @&(~1)seared short ribs{}, then pour in @dry red wine{1 1/2%cup}(355 mL) and scrape the base clean.

>> step: 40 min high pressure, natural release 15 min
Pressure cook @&(~1)pot{} with @beef stock{1 1/2%cup}(355 mL), @thyme{6%sprigs}, lid on and valve sealed: ~come to pressure{15%min}, then ~pressure cook{40%min} on high and ~natural release{15%min}, which keeps working on the collagen after the heat is off.

>> step: skim, reduce lid off 15 min
Skim @&(~1)pot{} of the fat that has risen, lift the ribs out, and ~reduce{15%min} the liquid on sauté with the lid off until it coats a spoon.
